{
 "version": 1,
 "about": "A corpus held in a cache: how the gate treats revocation and expiry when the hub can and cannot be reached. An expiry the device holds is honoured by its own clock, online or not; revocation waits for the next contact. standing.revalidated_at is when the licence block was last confirmed by the hub; standing.reachable is whether the hub answered the last time it was asked. A clock that is set back does not reopen a licence: the gate reads no time earlier than revalidated_at or standing.witnessed_at (the latest time the cache has seen on the device's own clock; absent means none).",
